1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,455
So I built this app called TrayHelper,
totally with Grok Bot.

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:06,636
What I can do is turn it on
for, say, Grok Bot,

3
00:00:06,727 --> 00:00:09,455
so that when I'm using Grok Bot

4
00:00:09,545 --> 00:00:13,000
and I close it,
the app doesn't shut down.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
It's still available
through the tray icon right here.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,182
I can click it and it opens.

7
00:00:19,273 --> 00:00:22,455
The same works for Cursor, because Cursor
doesn't natively support this feature.

8
00:00:22,545 --> 00:00:28,364
If I want to just close the window
but keep Cursor running in the background,

9
00:00:28,364 --> 00:00:31,364
I just click once, and it works now.

10
00:00:31,455 --> 00:00:36,000
So I hope Grok Bot and Cursor
can support this feature in the future,

11
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:40,909
because it really helps keep
a tidy window and a tidy taskbar.

12
00:00:41,727 --> 00:00:45,364
It also supports other apps
that don't even have this feature,

13
00:00:45,909 --> 00:00:50,545
for example Excel. People usually
don't expect Excel to have this,

14
00:00:50,636 --> 00:00:53,091
but I can open Excel and close it,

15
00:00:53,182 --> 00:00:57,182
and look, Excel is in the tray —
I don't think you've seen this before.

16
00:00:57,273 --> 00:01:00,455
And with a click, you can open it again.

17
00:01:01,273 --> 00:01:02,909
The UI looks good here, too.

18
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,455
I can hide it to the tray, quit Excel,

19
00:01:06,545 --> 00:01:09,091
turn off this feature,
or just open TrayHelper.

20
00:01:09,545 --> 00:01:12,727
I'm super amazed by
what Grok Bot can do here.

